# ============================================================================
# Frozen MutationIR / conflict order contract v1 — contract-freeze gate.
#
# Architecture §8 (MutationIR and transactional transformation), §26 (contract
# freeze), §27 (MUTATE lane owns structural/mutation), §30.5 (MutationIR
# verification obligations).
#
# This spec is the gate for the MUTATE lane deliverable. Like the ID-TAG, MAP
# and QUERY gates it proves four separate things, because round-tripping alone
# is not enough for a frozen contract:
#
#   1. EXACT BYTES — encoder output equals a hand-derived golden vector. This is
#      what actually freezes the format; a round-trip test alone passes happily
#      even if encoder and decoder drift together.
#   2. ROUND TRIP — decode(encode(x)) reconstructs x for every record shape.
#   3. REJECTION — malformed, truncated, cross-typed, wrong-version and
#      structurally-invalid buffers are refused rather than silently coerced,
#      on ENCODE as well as decode.
#   4. ORDER — §8.4's six-key conflict order is total, strict, and enforced on
#      the wire. For a transactional plan this is the important half: a plan
#      stored out of order does not fail loudly, it commits a DIFFERENT snapshot
#      depending on which evaluator walked it.
# ============================================================================

